@gubenkoved this is because the flex element created by `st.write` is full width in the column so aligning it right doesn't have an effect. Also, in the example where you are using a horizontal container, you would need content alignment right within the container to move the text to the right side within the flex element. The horizontal alignment feature is the alignment of the whole element including its wrapper (which is full width for `st.write`). 

We have some discussion about this here as well https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/issues/12127

If you use `st.markdown` instead of `st.write` then you can set `width="content"` and achieve the right alignment.

