The same problem occures with the usage of `st.experimental_singleton`
I have an another workaround:

```python
@st.experimental_singleton
def make_singleton_class(original_class):
    return original_class
```
Which can be use as an annotation for the newly created classes
```python
from enum import Enum

@make_singleton_class
class Cica(Enum):
    VALUE = 4
    
@st.experimental_singleton
def get_cica():
    return Cica.VALUE
    
st.header(get_cica() == Cica.VALUE) # this will print 'True' always
```

I think this can be a default operation for all `Enum`.

Another solution can be that streamlit `cache` or `experimental_singleton` accept classes too, where
```python
@st.experimental_singleton
class Cica(Enum):
    VALUE = 4
```
works like `make_singleton_class` defined above

